          "candidate_block": 1,
          "candidate_line_count": 3,
          "center_error": 0.126,
          "text": "Measures for Domestic Project Business\nManagement of CCECC Fuzhou Survey & Design Institute Co."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "chapter_heading",
          "source_block": 3,
          "candidate_block": 3,
          "candidate_line_count": 1,
          "center_error": 0.111,
          "text": "Chapter 1 General Provisions"
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 4,
          "candidate_block": 4,
          "candidate_line_count": 7,
          "center_error": 18.097,
          "text": "Article 1 In accordance with the guiding opinions on high­quality\nbusiness operations of the joint­stock company, and considering the relevant\nrequirements of the Group Company's \"Implementation Rules for High­Quality\nBusiness Operations (Trial)\" (Zhong Tu Jing Ying 2024 No. 341), these\nMeasures are formulated to comprehensively improve project business\nquality, effectively manage the Company's domestic business operations, and\nstandardize business procedures and workflows."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 8,
          "candidate_block": 5,
          "candidate_line_count": 3,
          "center_error": 20.595,
          "text": "Article 2 The projects referred to in these Measures include consulting,\nsurvey, design, supervision, EPC, and other types of business undertaken by\nthe Company through direct commission or bidding."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 10,
          "candidate_block": 6,
          "candidate_line_count": 3,
          "center_error": 21.308,
          "text": "Article 3 In principle, business undertaking shall follow the procedure of\nfirst conducting project evaluation, then applying for approval, and finally\nsigning the contract."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 12,
          "candidate_block": 7,
          "candidate_line_count": 8,
          "center_error": 20.535,
          "text": "Article 4 When carrying out project business undertaking, factors such\nas the Company's development strategy, business direction, responsibility\ncost, production and technical capabilities, and current status shall be\ncomprehensively considered. According to the workflow specified in these\nMeasures, tasks including \"information tracking, project evaluation and\napplication, bid document preparation and review, contract negotiation,\ncontract review and signing, client service during project implementation, and\nproject follow­up\" shall be completed."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "chapter_heading",
          "source_block": 17,
          "candidate_block": 8,
          "candidate_line_count": 1,
          "center_error": 0.127,
          "text": "Chapter 2 Relevant Responsibilities"
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 18,
          "candidate_block": 9,
          "candidate_line_count": 3,
          "center_error": 16.623,
          "text": "Article 5 The Business Development Department is the management\ndepartment for the Company's domestic project business operations,\nresponsible for the layout and expansion of the institute­wide business market."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 20,
          "candidate_block": 10,
          "candidate_line_count": 2,
          "center_error": 20.602,
          "text": "Article 6 The relevant personnel involved in project business operations\nand their main responsibilities are shown in Table 1:"
        },
